From 35d17f52e1c04bd4b8118b91e92bf35601327336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rocky <rocky@zeroclaw>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): attach to a running /ws/chat turn from another
 socket

A turn's only live viewer is the socket that started it: after a client
restart the turn keeps running but its steps are lost. Every frame a turn
sends is now also recorded per session (ws_turn_watch, streamed deltas
merged). A new socket on the session sends {"type":"attach"} and gets
{type:"attached", running, turn_id, replayed}, the frames so far, then the
rest live up to the terminal done/aborted/error frame. Read-only: text
frames get ATTACHED_READ_ONLY. No running turn: {type:"attached",
running:false}.
